@ 2026-08-28T23:00:00Z chatgpt temprun temporal-learning-bootstrap
= Bootstrap temprun as a Temporal learning lab for distributed-systems and agent-runtime interview preparation.

+ C claim settled temprun-is-learning-lab : temprun exists primarily to learn Temporal and durable distributed execution, not to become a polished agent framework.
+ C claim settled temporal-primitives-should-stay-visible : Early implementation should expose Temporal Workflows, Activities, Signals, Queries, retries, task queues, and Child Workflows directly rather than hide them behind custom abstractions.
+ C claim settled fake-agents-first : Initial agents should be fake Activities so Temporal behavior can be studied without LLM/provider complexity.
+ C claim settled failure-experiments-are-core : Retry, replay, worker crash, cancellation, idempotency, and durable waiting should be learned through explicit experiments.
+ C claim settled workflow-activity-boundary-is-central : Workflow code coordinates durable state and must remain replay-safe while external or nondeterministic work belongs in Activities.

+ K decision accepted use-chronelle-working-memory-shape : Use MEMORY.md for current status, journal/YYYY-MM-DD.md for detailed paper trail, and .memory/records/YYYY/MM/DD/*.chron for compact durable source records.
+ K commitment active bootstrap-temporal-project : Create the minimal Python Temporal project and first ResearchWorkflow.
+ K commitment active implement-parallel-agent-fanout : Run three fake agent Activities in parallel and synthesize their results.
+ K commitment active add-controlled-retry-experiment : Add controlled Activity failure plus Temporal RetryPolicy and observe retry behavior.
+ K commitment proposed add-signal-approval : Add durable human approval via Signal after milestone 1.
+ K commitment proposed run-worker-crash-experiments : Kill and restart workers at adversarial points and document observed behavior.

